[ ] Script the specification release $From 2026-10-13: v0.3.0 was cut by hand (changelog heading for the pending entries, every schema \$id moved, annotated tag on main, release fast-forwarded to publish clearhead.dev), and two commits had no changelog entry until release time. A scripts/release <version> does the mechanical steps and refuses when a commit since the last tag touched spec files without a changelog entry; choosing the version and deciding to publish stay with Darrion. Releasing includes adopting it, in the same session: Core declares the new version (Cargo.toml metadata, schema URLs, CHANGELOG) and the platform pins both, with this checkout on release. v0.3.0 sat unadopted for a day (2026-10-14).$ ^2026-10-13T07:54 #01a13441-b0e0-7ea1-9deb-eadc13a16cf1
[ ] Specify close as a state change and archive by root tree =ci-spec $Step 1 of platform =close-individually (platform docs/close-individually-proposal.md, Decisions 58 and 59, approved by Darrion 2026-11-02). Specification text only, for a release the steward tags afterwards; do not bump schema ids or tag. No clearhead CLI here; the gate is .sandbox/gate. Do not touch habit fixtures or Habit text. Leave this action open; the steward closes it. (1) workspace.md Archival item 2: closing a line changes state in place and does not move it. Only archive and unarchive move lines, always a whole root tree (a root and everything below it): archive takes a closed root whose whole tree is closed; unarchive takes a root in the completed file; a child is refused and its root named. Closed lines in the active file are ordinary; a parent link inside an archived tree is kept. (2) linting.md W002: reword from 'cannot be marked as closed' to report the contradiction (a closed parent with an open child), and remove the third example, \[x] Parent over \[_] child, which has no open child and is not flagged. W002 and W003 stay warnings. (3) schemas/transaction_request.schema.json: complete-action and cancel-action become single operations on the named action: stamp state and completed_at in place, no cascade, no detach, no file move. Add reopen-action: state not_started, date cleared, active file only, refused if archived. Fix every description that promises cascade or file move. (4) Update examples/transactions and explanations/data_workflows.md to match; add a valid reopen-action example. (5) Add a dated changelog entry under today's date with no version heading, in the file's style. Done means the gate passes and a grep for cascade, file move and moves in these files finds no stale promise. Core will fail against these until its own step; that is expected and not part of this action. Added by the steward on push-back, from the proposal's Close section: (6) schemas/transaction_result.schema.json: completed and cancelled outcomes carry no children and require open_children, the canonical ids left open beneath the action, empty when none; reopened carries neither; only deleted keeps children. Examples, data_workflows.md and the changelog follow. (7) update-action refuses a closed target altogether (proposal, How-level calls: update keeps refusing closed actions and terminal states), stated in the updateAction description and the changelog.$ !2 ^2026-11-02T02:42 #01a19a23-25a1-7b73-b1cc-2b11d2a19de4
